  "design_notes": [
    "Reference crossbar separates read/write datapaths and address admission, with configurable thread/accept/issue limits and ID routing.",
    "This implementation intentionally supports one outstanding transaction per source and target per direction. Ownership state restores response source IDs; exclusive requests are rejected DECERR to avoid shared downstream exclusive-ID ambiguity.",
    "Round-robin arbitration occurs for pending address descriptors independently for reads and writes. Whole invalid bursts are locally completed using LEN-based framing. No third-party RTL is copied."
  ]
